1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:03,200
Every stock chart hides a line.

2
00:00:03,300 --> 00:00:06,200
Connect the highs, or the lows —
and you get a diagonal.

3
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:09,500
When price breaks it… things happen.

4
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:13,000
There are more than two thousand
stocks worth watching.

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,200
You can't watch them all. Nobody can.

6
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,500
This is Diago. Every night it redraws
the trendlines of 2,259 stocks.

7
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:31,500
And the moment a stock closes
above its diagonal —

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,200
you get the alert. With a score.

9
00:00:41,200 --> 00:00:43,500
It works the other way too.

10
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:48,000
A stock falls hard — all the way back
to its rising support line…

11
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:52,000
holds it, and bounces.
That's Diago's strongest setup.

12
00:00:56,200 --> 00:01:00,500
Every signal gets a confidence score —
calibrated on 72,000 historical setups.

13
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:05,000
And every signal is tracked, publicly,
from the day it prints.

14
00:01:05,500 --> 00:01:11,000
Winners… and losers.
Nothing deleted. Ever.

15
00:01:12,300 --> 00:01:17,000
Diago. Your ranked shortlist, ready
every morning before the market opens.

16
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:21,500
Seven days free. Then five dollars a month.

17
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:27,200
Simulated results. Statistics, not promises.
Never investment advice.
